## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design multisource joins with simple, robust windowing and per-topic state management in KCNA. It exercises offset handling, at-least-once guarantees, and failure/restart semantics without requiring complex infrastructure.

## Key Concepts
- Per-topic buffering keyed by orderId
- Windowed join with 45s bound
- Atomic offset commits on emission
- Handling of partials and expirations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode sketch
class Joiner {
  constructor(windowMs) { this.window = windowMs; this.buffers = new Map(); }
  onMessage(topic, msg, ts) {
    const key = msg.orderId;
    const bucket = this.buffers.get(key) || {orders: null, payments: null, shipments: null, times: []};
    bucket[topic] = msg;
    bucket.times.push(ts);
    if (bucket.orders && bucket.payments && bucket.shipments) {
      const w = Math.max(...bucket.times) - Math.min(...bucket.times);
      if (w <= this.window) this.emit(key, bucket);
    }
    this.buffers.set(key, bucket);
  }
  emit(key, bucket) {
    // publish to fulfillments and commit offsets for involved messages
    // prune buffers after emit
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adjust for late events beyond 45s?
- How to test drift and ensure exactly-once-like behavior in logs?
- How would you scale state without a single hot key?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of cross-region consistency, exactly-once semantics, and failover handling—critical skills for building regulated audit systems that require high reliability and compliance.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-region replication and exactly-once delivery guarantees
- Idempotent sinks with durable deduplication state
- Transactional outbox pattern for atomic offset commits
- Mapping local partition offsets to a globally ordered sequence
- Replay resilience and failover recovery strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: Exactly-once consumer with transactional outbox
async function processEvent(event, consumer, producer) {
  const globalId = `${event.region}||${event.partition}||${event.offset}`;

  // Check dedup store
  if (await dedupStore.exists(globalId)) {
    await consumer.commitOffsets([{ topic: event.topic, partition: event.partition, offset: event.offset + 1 }]);
    return;
  }

  // Transaction: write audit + commit offset
  await producer.beginTransaction();
  try {
    await writeToAuditTable(globalId, event.payload);
    await dedupStore.set(globalId, { ttl: 86400 });
    await producer.sendOffsetsToTransaction([{ topic: event.topic, partition: event.partition, offset: event.offset + 1 }], consumerGroupId);
    await producer.commitTransaction();
  } catch (err) {
    await producer.abortTransaction();
    throw err;
  }
}
```
